{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — confirmed defect (Phase 1)\n\n**Proven root cause.** The completion verifier's deterministic **prefetch** reads\nverdict-bearing working-tree file bodies from the LIVE checkout (B), not the `--ref`-pinned\ncode snapshot (A). `completion_prefetch.assemble_prefetch(spec, repo_root=...)` is called by\n`gate_ops.completion_precheck` with `repo_root=ctx.repo_root` — which is the TICKET-store /\nlive checkout root (the workflow threads the live root; the pinned code snapshot is a SEPARATE\nmaterialized tree, exposed via `current_code_root()` / `cfg.repo_path`). `assemble_prefetch`\nthen does its working-tree reads through that same `repo_root`:\n`_read_body(repo_root, path)` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_prefetch.py:329-334`) and\n`_discover_test_globs(repo_root, …)` (`:338-357`). It never consults `current_code_root()` /\n`resolve_code_root`, so even inside an attested gate that correctly pinned A, the prefetched\n`<prefetched_file_contents>` block contains B's bytes, and those bytes are injected into the\nverifier's context as evidence it judges criteria against.\n\nEvery OTHER verdict-bearing code read is correctly pinned to A: the agentic verifier's\nread_file/search_files resolve via `cfg.repo_path` / `use_code_root(handle.path)`\n(`gate_source.gate_read_root`); `completion_reconcile` resolves citations via `cfg.repo_path`\n(`gate_ops.py:290`); `verified_at_sha` and the completion signature bind to `handle.sha` = A\n(`gate_source.annotate_result`). The transition-close drift guard compares the live HEAD/ref\nagainst the verified sha — the contract-permitted, one-way \"reject/retry stale work\" live\ncomparison, not verdict evidence. So the account is a SINGLE leak: the prefetch working-tree\nreads.\n\n`referencing_commit_diffs` reads via `git -C <repo_root> show <sha>`; a commit diff is\nimmutable content addressed by an immutable SHA (identical from any clone that holds the\nobject) and the materialized snapshot has no `.git`, so that read is intentionally left on the\nlive repo's object store — it is not live-mutable checkout evidence.\n\n**Proof (runtime, dynamic hypothesis).** Divergent A/B experiment: a live checkout dir B and a\nseparate pinned snapshot dir A each hold `target.py` with deliberately different content;\nticket `file_impact` declares `target.py` (only the ticket-state boundary stubbed). Entering\nthe REAL `gate_source.gate_read_root(SnapshotHandle(path=A, source=attested))` context (which\nactivates `use_code_root(A)` — verified: `current_code_root()` == A inside the block) and then\ncalling the REAL `assemble_prefetch(spec, repo_root=B)` exactly as `completion_precheck` does,\nthe emitted `<prefetched_file_contents>` contained `LIVE_B_CONTENT` and did NOT contain\n`PINNED_A_CONTENT`. Predicted-if-true (reads B) observed; predicted-if-false (reads A) ruled\nout. The mechanism fires at runtime.\n\n**Defect origin (caused_by).** `a9dd-bbc7-f549-4fc2` — \"prefetch file_impact into verifier\ncontext\", landed as commit `6d343d13626c`. This is the commit that added `completion_prefetch`\nand wired it into `completion_precheck`, reading code through the threaded `repo_root` without\nresolving the pinned code root. The pinned-code-root primitives (`resolve_code_root`,\n`use_code_root`) already existed at a9dd's parent (verified: both present at `6d343d13626c^`),\nso this is an unmet-obligation / incomplete-implementation miss in a9dd, not a regression of\nolder code — attribution is to a9dd's introducing commit, and `git blame` on the implicated\nlines names a9dd directly (not a carrier). Close class: `plan_defect`.\n\n**Disposition.** Confirmed `defect` (violates the pinned-`--ref` code-read contract stated in\nthis ticket and established by `sedate-villainous-teledu` / `resolve_code_root`'s documented\npurpose). Fix is a localized re-root of the prefetch's working-tree reads to the pinned code\nroot; RED regression test + fix to follow under RED→GREEN."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787938441048492001,"uuid":"8c483b7f-6fe7-45b2-9632-bfd808843eb9"}